There is hereby established an Institute called the Brunei National Energy Research Institute which shall be a body corporate with perpetual succession and a common seal and shall, by that name, be capable of(a) suing and being sued;

(b) acquiring, owning, holding, developing or disposing of property both and immovable; and

(c) doing all such other acts or things as a body corporate may lawfully do. seal.

(1) The functions of the Institute shall include the following(a} to create and develop a world class premier energy research and capabilities in Brunei Darussalam;

(b) to conduct research and development in all fields of energy energy technology development and verification;

(c) to initiate and undertake or enter into contractual testing, research or development projects for the purpose of its

(d) to promote and commercialise and enable deployment of research and innovative solutions into the local and international marketin the field of energy; {e) to provide financial assistance for appropriate and approved energy and development activities; If} to promote collaborative links between governments, businesses, industries, universities and societies in identifying and exploiting key niches for developments and progress in energy; {g) to encourage a multi-disciplinary and holistic approach to problemin the field of energy;

(h) to encourage a culture that is energy-conscious and committed towards energy security and environmental sustainability; {i) to disseminate, share and promote research findings through . published papers, seminars and conferences, in the field of energy;

(j) to promote research and development among youths, and to develop public awareness of the importance of energy research and development in Brunei Darussalam; and {k} to do all such things as may be necessary, incidental or conducive to the attainment of all or any of its functions and powers.

(2) In addition to the functions specified in subsection (1), the Minister may assign other functions to the Institute and the Institute shall be deemed to be fulfilling the purposes of this Order.

(3) In carrying out its functions, the Institute shall - (a} have regard to the needs of Brunei Darussalam and its resources; and

(b) promote developments, commercial applications that increase economic growth, productivity and employment opportunities in Brunei of Institute.

For the discharge of its functions or duties under this Order or any other law, the Institute may, from time to time, raise loans from the with the approval of the Minister, raise loans from banks and financial institutions (whether in Brunei Darussalam or elsewhere) by(a} mortgage, overdraft or otherwise;

(b) whether legal or equitable, on any property vested in the on any revenue receivable by the Institute under this Order or any written law; or

(c) the creation and issue or debentures or bonds or other instruments.
